			"type": "text",
			"text": "Pholidosaurus was a pholidosaurid crocodylomorph which lived in the Early Cretaceous of Europe, discovered in the Obernkirchen Sandstone of Germany in 1830. Its name means “horny-scaled lizard” in reference to osteoderms and grew to about the same size as the extant gharial. Pholidosaurus was a member of Pholidosauridae, a crocodylomorph family distantly related to true crocodylians, characterized by typically longirostrine snouts."
